Cloudflare CEO @eastdakota states that agents surpassing human traffic online is just the beginning. He believes bot-generated traffic could eventually be 1,000 times greater than human traffic.

He notes that bot traffic has already exceeded human traffic in the first half of 2026, much earlier than his previous predictions. These agents can visit thousands of websites to find the best prices, delivery options, and services, driving a huge amount of Internet consumption.

@eastdakota: "Welp, that happened faster than I predicted. Thought it would be end of 2027, then early 2027, but agentic traffic growing so fast that bots have now passed human traffic online for the first time in the Internet's history."

Maggie's Refuel is a new high-end gas station opening soon in Los Angeles that will offer freshly baked pastries, lattes on tap, pressed juice, and other premium convenience items.

Jordi comments that everything inside the modern gas station feels almost like poison, highlighting a humorous or critical view of the environment.

@karine_hsu describes Maggie's Refuel as a brand aiming to modernize and innovate the gas station experience, combining elements of Autogrill and 7-Eleven Japan, with offerings like matcha, local croissants, premium consumer packaged goods, and soft-serve cones, alongside gas or electric vehicle charging.

